      }
    ],
    "start_event": "t=0: commander at ORV receives report of two additional T-55s and two trucks; B Security is not answering.",
    "source_facts": [
      "BLUE: three rifle sections, one organic weapons section, one attached section with exactly two modern medium-range anti-armour weapons.",
      "Charlie section is already divided into A/B/C security elements and a navigation team; it is not an extra full section at ORV.",
      "Main body and attachments at ORV, A at VP, navigation at RP, C on the southern cut-off; B was at the northern cut-off.",
      "Four T-55s and two large trucks are confirmed; dismounted infantry numbers and B Security casualties are unknown.",
      "Clear night with full moon, dense vegetation, stream passable to foot but not vehicles away from the bridge.",
      "The original briefing estimated first light in 12 hours; over three hours plus recce have elapsed, so remaining time is unspecified.",
      "No current UAS support, allocated artillery, available CAS or timely reinforcements are established."
    ],
    "modeling_assumptions": [
      "BLUE total 35 personnel: Alpha 8 + Bravo 8 + Charlie 8 (four pairs) + HQ 3 + organic GPMG crews 4 + attached AT crews 4.",
      "One generic SAW per automatic rifleman proxies the C9 role; two generic GPMGs proxy the unspecified organic weapons section.",
      "Exactly two generic ATGM launchers, one per 2-person crew, with three rounds each; model and ammunition are assumptions.",
      "RED baseline assumes one 27-person infantry platoon: three sections of eight and HQ of three, already dismounted between two trucks.",
      "Truck carrying capacity is not evidence for two full enemy platoons. Infantry strength is deliberately an explicit sensitivity assumption.",
      "Two B Security survivors with a failed radio and standing rally plan are a possible ground truth, not a confirmed report.",
      "Reported wounded have no quantified losses applied because the source gives neither identities nor counts.",
      "T-55s use generic legacy tank gun/protection mechanics; they are not calibrated T-55 models. Tank ammunition 15 AP + 20 HE is an assumption.",
      "Vehicle crew numbers are descriptive equipment metadata, not extra dismounted formations. Trucks are unarmed logistics entities.",
      "All initial positions are approximate Figure 1 placements. Unit footprints and full-moon NIGHT sensor multipliers are authoring assumptions.",
      "Both sides use the same generic rifle-section weapons, sensors and movement; actual RED infantry equipment is unspecified.",
      "A Security is an actively engaging early-warning screen, not a silent observation-only post; this is the selected engine posture.",
      "Retains the user-approved widened terrain (32 m stream, 16 m road, 44 x 12 m bridge); these are schematic dimensions, not the PDF bridge dimensions.",
      "The southern map exit is a local proxy for progress toward off-map M Company, not M Company itself or its main river crossing."
    ],
